    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39686" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pŭtĕālis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a well</i>, <i>well-</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">undae,</span>”
				<i>well-water</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. Ib.
					391</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lymphae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					6, 1178</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aquae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 43, 1, 20, § 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fons,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					11, 3, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">unda,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 1,
					5, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pocula,</span>”
				<i>of spring-water</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Juvenc. 2, 259</span></i>
			; cf. puteanus.</div>
